# Office Network using VLANs and Router-on-a-Stick

This project demonstrates how to design and configure a small office network using VLANs and a router-on-a-stick topology in Cisco Packet Tracer.

## Project Structure

- 3 VLANs: HR (10), Finance (20), IT (30)
- 3 Switches (2960), one for each department
- 1 Router (2911), connected via trunk links
- PCs configured with static IPs and gateways
- Ping tests used to verify inter-VLAN connectivity

## Tools Used

- Cisco Packet Tracer
- Basic Networking commands (show, ping, ip config)
- Manual VLAN and IP setup

